{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-10-07T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"What if a forest could keep you guessing at every turn? At Puzzlewood, near Coleford in the Forest of Dean, England, winding paths lead through twisted trees, moss-covered rocks and deep stone ravines. Its unusual rock formations, known as scowles, are natural geological features that were exposed and modified over time and later exploited for iron ore mining during the Roman period and possibly earlier. In 1848, a worker discovered more than 3,000 Roman-era coins hidden in earthenware jars inside a rock cavity, turning the woodland into a real-life treasure hunt.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.ForestofDean_EN-IN7618980046_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.ForestofDean_EN-IN7618980046_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Puzzled? Follow the trail","Title":"Moss-covered rocks in Puzzlewood, Forest of Dean, Gloucestershire, England","Copyright":"© Fulcanelli_AOS/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/51.812183,-2.516615/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=51.812183,-2.516615;S9;Forest of Dean, Gloucestershire, England&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261007_ForestofDean\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Puzzlewood+England&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261006_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261007_ForestofDean"},"Ssd":"20261007","Name":"ForestofDean","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"7618980046","FullDateString":"7 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"What if a mountain range could show you its geological history in stripes? At Zhangye National Geopark in China, the rocks do exactly that. Ridges roll across the landscape in bands of red, orange, yellow, brown and other earthy tones. Known as the Danxia landform, this striking landscape was shaped by layers of sedimentary rock deposited over geological time. Tectonic forces later lifted and folded the rocks, while weathering and erosion carved them into ridges, cliffs, gullies and peaks.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.DanxiaLandform_EN-IN7469232165_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.DanxiaLandform_EN-IN7469232165_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Earth's story in stripes","Title":"Danxia landform, Zhangye National Geopark, Gansu, China","Copyright":"© Weiquan Lin/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/38.966774,100.04408/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=38.966774,100.04408;S9;Zhangye National Geopark, Gansu, China&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261006_DanxiaLandform\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=International+Geodiversity+Day&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261005_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261006_DanxiaLandform"},"Ssd":"20261006","Name":"DanxiaLandform","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"7469232165","FullDateString":"6 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"What can a 70-centimetre-tall bird teach us about life? Quite a lot. The Adélie penguin offers a lesson plan packed with resourcefulness, resilience and a little mischief. Found along the Antarctic coast, the species was named after Adèle, the wife of French explorer Jules Dumont d'Urville, during the expedition that encountered the penguins in 1840.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AdelieTeacher_EN-IN7367199250_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AdelieTeacher_EN-IN7367199250_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Slide into adventure","Title":"Adélie penguins, Antarctica","Copyright":"© Otto Plantema/Minden Pictures","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"Adélie penguins do not have teeth, but instead have sharp, backward-pointing spikes called papillae on their tongues and the roofs of their mouths.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261005_AdelieTeacher\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Adelie+penguins&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261004_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261005_AdelieTeacher"},"Ssd":"20261005","Name":"AdelieTeacher","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"7367199250","FullDateString":"5 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"First, you build a rocket. Then you ask it to leave Earth, fly to the moon, survive the trip and bring its spacecraft home. Simple, right? Well, not quite. World Space Week, observed every 4-10 October, celebrates the science that makes missions like this possible. The United Nations established the observance in 1999 to commemorate Sputnik 1's launch on 4 October 1957, and the entry into force of the Outer Space Treaty on 10 October 1967. This year's theme, 'Rocket Revolution,' focuses on the evolving technology driving space exploration.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.ArtemisRocket_EN-IN7247754075_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.ArtemisRocket_EN-IN7247754075_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":false},"Headline":"The universe is calling","Title":"Artemis I moon rocket at Launch Complex 39B, Kennedy Space Center, Florida, United States","Copyright":"© EVA MARIE UZCATEGUI/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/28.522254,-80.68167/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=28.522254,-80.68167;S9;Kennedy Space Center, Florida, United States&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261004_ArtemisRocket\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=World+Space+Week&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261003_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261004_ArtemisRocket"},"Ssd":"20261004","Name":"ArtemisRocket","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"7247754075","FullDateString":"4 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"The season of big meals, bigger bellies and stocking up for winter is here. In Alaska, United States, brown bears at Lake Clark National Park and Preserve make the most of the food still available in October. They feed on fish, sedges, berries, roots, clams and other foods to build up fat reserves. Some can weigh more than 450 kilograms before entering their dens for hibernation. That stored fat helps them survive the winter, when they do not eat or drink.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.GrizzlySwim_EN-IN7120112042_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.GrizzlySwim_EN-IN7120112042_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Catch, eat, repeat","Title":"Brown bear in Silver Salmon Creek, Lake Clark National Park and Preserve, Alaska, United States","Copyright":"© Danny Green/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/61.147081,-153.734242/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=61.147081,-153.734242;S9;Lake Clark National Park and Preserve, Alaska, United States&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261003_GrizzlySwim\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Brown+bear&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261002_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261003_GrizzlySwim"},"Ssd":"20261003","Name":"GrizzlySwim","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"7120112042","FullDateString":"3 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Not every freedom fighter carried a weapon. He carried an idea. Gandhi Jayanti marks the birth of Mohandas Karamchand Gandhi, born in Porbandar, India, in 1869. He became a key leader of India's independence movement through satyagraha, his philosophy of truth and non-violent resistance. His 1930 Salt March showed how something as ordinary as salt could become a powerful symbol of protest. His influence eventually reached far beyond India, inspiring movements built around peaceful resistance.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.GandhiJayanti2026_EN-IN7052712451_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.GandhiJayanti2026_EN-IN7052712451_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"The man who made peace powerful","Title":"Mahatma Gandhi statue at the Sabarmati Ashram in Ahmedabad, Gujarat","Copyright":"© Kandarp Gupta/Alamy","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/23.060703,72.580301/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=23.060703,72.580301;S9;Sabarmati Ashram, Ahmedabad, Gujarat&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261002_GandhiJayanti2026\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Gandhi+Jayanti&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261001_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261002_GandhiJayanti2026"},"Ssd":"20261002","Name":"GandhiJayanti2026","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"7052712451","FullDateString":"2 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"What if two architects worked on the same house but saw it differently? Nathmal Ki Haveli in Jaisalmer offers the answer in carved sandstone. Built in the late 19th century, the haveli is associated with architect brothers Hathi and Lulu, who worked independently on its two sides. They look similar at first, but their fine details differ.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.NathmaljiHaveli2026_EN-IN9027003376_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.NathmaljiHaveli2026_EN-IN9027003376_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Carved from two points of view","Title":"View into the sky from Nathmal Ki Haveli courtyard, Jaisalmer, Rajasthan","Copyright":"© Emad Aljumah/Moment/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/26.91358,70.925537/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=26.91358,70.925537;S9;Jaisalmer, Rajasthan&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261001_NathmaljiHaveli2026\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Jaisalmer+Rajasthan&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260930_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261001_NathmaljiHaveli2026"},"Ssd":"20261001","Name":"NathmaljiHaveli2026","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"9027003376","FullDateString":"1 Oct, 2026"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"How do we know what Earth looked like long before humans appeared? Fossils provide many clues. From dinosaurs to tiny marine organisms, these remnants of the past preserve snapshots of ancient worlds that no longer exist.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AmmoniteFossils_EN-IN8565946131_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AmmoniteFossils_EN-IN8565946131_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Spirals through time","Title":"Ammonite fossils from the Jurassic Period","Copyright":"© J Nemchinova/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"A fossil doesn't have to be a bone. Tracks, burrows, nests and other traces of ancient life can become fossils too.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261014_AmmoniteFossils\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Ammonite+fossils&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261013_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261014_AmmoniteFossils"},"Ssd":"20261014","Name":"AmmoniteFossils","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"8565946131","FullDateString":"14 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Water seems to be everywhere at Plitvice Lakes National Park in Croatia. Sixteen terraced lakes are linked by a network of waterfalls, streams and cascades that wind through forested limestone canyons. The constantly changing colours of the water, ranging from emerald green to deep blue, are shaped by minerals, sunlight and ever-changing reflections. Established in 1949, Plitvice Lakes is Croatia's oldest and largest national park. The landscape is famous for its tufa barriers, natural limestone formations created as mineral-rich water deposits calcium carbonate over centuries. These barriers continue to grow and change, gradually transforming the park's waterfalls and lakes.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.PlitviceAutumn_EN-IN8498813927_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.PlitviceAutumn_EN-IN8498813927_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A symphony in blue and green","Title":"Plitvice Lakes National Park, Croatia","Copyright":"© Jan Wlodarczyk/Alamy","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/44.866465,15.581867/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=44.866465,15.581867;S9;Plitvice Lakes National Park, Croatia&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261013_PlitviceAutumn\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Plitvice+Lakes+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261012_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261013_PlitviceAutumn"},"Ssd":"20261013","Name":"PlitviceAutumn","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"8498813927","FullDateString":"13 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"What do you get when a railway, a lifeboat station and a seaside day out meet at the water's edge? Mumbles Pier. Stretching 255 metres into Swansea Bay, this Victorian landmark opened on 10 May 1898 and has been part of the Welsh coast ever since.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.MumblesSwansea2026_EN-IN8292362227_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.MumblesSwansea2026_EN-IN8292362227_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Pier-ing into the past","Title":"Mumbles Pier, Swansea, Wales","Copyright":"© Helen Hotson/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/51.5755,-4.001746/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=51.5755,-4.001746;S9;Mumbles, Swansea, Wales&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261012_MumblesSwansea2026\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Mumbles+Pier+Wales&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261011_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261012_MumblesSwansea2026"},"Ssd":"20261012","Name":"MumblesSwansea2026","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"8292362227","FullDateString":"12 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Surrounded by a patchwork of red, orange and gold, Glade Creek Grist Mill stands above the rocky waters of Glade Creek in West Virginia's Babcock State Park, United States. Although it looks like a relic from the pioneer era, the mill is actually a carefully crafted tribute to Appalachia's milling heritage.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.BabcockSP_EN-IN8141556742_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.BabcockSP_EN-IN8141556742_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Where autumn turns the wheel","Title":"Glade Creek Grist Mill, Babcock State Park, West Virginia, United States","Copyright":"© dszc/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/37.996698,-80.977125/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=37.996698,-80.977125;S9;Babcock State Park, West Virginia, United States&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261011_BabcockSP\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Babcock+State+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261010_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261011_BabcockSP"},"Ssd":"20261011","Name":"BabcockSP","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"8141556742","FullDateString":"11 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"World Migratory Bird Day celebrates one of nature's greatest journeys. Observed each year in May and October, the global campaign reflects migration patterns around the world and highlights the importance of protecting the habitats and flyways that birds depend on. 'Every Bird Counts—Your Observations Matter!' is the 2026 theme, emphasising how observations by individuals and communities can contribute to bird research, monitoring and conservation, helping scientists better understand migration.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.CormorantsFlight_EN-IN8066576004_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.CormorantsFlight_EN-IN8066576004_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Life along the flyway","Title":"Double-crested cormorants over Monterey Bay, California, United States","Copyright":"© Hiroya Minakuchi/Minden Pictures","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"Bird migration can take many forms: some birds travel north or south, while others move to different elevations or habitats.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261010_CormorantsFlight\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=World+Migratory+Bird+Day&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261009_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261010_CormorantsFlight"},"Ssd":"20261010","Name":"CormorantsFlight","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"8066576004","FullDateString":"10 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Just off the coast of Corsica, France, the Sanguinaires Islands rise from the Mediterranean as a small archipelago of four rugged, rocky islands. Viewed from a historic watchtower, they sit at the entrance to the Gulf of Ajaccio. Steep cliffs, centuries-old landmarks and sweeping sea views have drawn visitors to the area for generations. Though the farthest island lies only about 2 kilometres from shore, the archipelago feels surprisingly remote, surrounded by open water and shaped by wind, waves and salt spray.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.IlesSanguinaires_EN-IN7867200667_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.IlesSanguinaires_EN-IN7867200667_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Corsica's rocky outposts","Title":"View of the Sanguinaires Islands from Corsica, France","Copyright":"© Francesco Riccardo Iacomino/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/41.88166,8.59779/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=41.88166,8.59779;S9;Sanguinaires Islands, Corsica, France&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261009_IlesSanguinaires\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Sanguinaires+Islands+Corsica&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261008_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261009_IlesSanguinaires"},"Ssd":"20261009","Name":"IlesSanguinaires","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"7867200667","FullDateString":"9 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Something has clearly crossed a line. Off the coast of Mayotte in the Indian Ocean, this octopus has adopted a defensive posture that says: whatever is approaching should reconsider its life choices.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.MayotteOctopus_EN-IN7698524475_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.MayotteOctopus_EN-IN7698524475_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Now you 'sea' me...","Title":"Octopus in defensive posture, Mayotte, Indian Ocean","Copyright":"© Gabriel Barathieu/Minden Pictures","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/-12.822125,45.148273/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&